# Zen holds all three work contexts in one process tree, so its budget is
# larger than a single-purpose browser's -- but it replaces three Firefox
# instances, so the total is still lower. Same idea as browser-firefox.slice;
# see the comments there.
#
# Resized 2026-08-26 from 5G/6G, which had drifted into a local 99-local.conf
# drop-in at 9G/10G because Zen outgrew the repo numbers (measured 8.58 GiB
# with 30 tabs, 28 pinned, ~20 sites under Fission). High=7G is a deliberate
# squeeze below that: the kernel keeps reclaiming Zen's cold pages into zram
# above 7G, which trades sluggish switches to stale tabs for ~1.5G given back
# to the rest of the machine. Max stays 10G so nothing gets OOM-killed at
# today's footprint. The drop-in is retired; these numbers are the only ones.
[Unit]
Description=Zen resource slice

[Slice]
MemoryHigh=7G
MemoryMax=10G
